\description{
Builds a graph of which of a segmentation's cells are neighbors, as a job, in the Spatial view: by the Delaunay triangulation of their centroids (its edges up to a longest length), each cell's k nearest (an edge when either is among the other's k), a radius, or contact in the segmentation's label raster (cells touching, or within a gap, with the boundary they share). Built over all the cells, a QC filter's or those in regions, never cells a review excluded. Recorded as a graph artifact; asking again answers it. Answers the cells and edges, the neighbors a cell, the cells without one, the pieces and the edges' lengths.
}
